  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Here, ${1}^{7}$ is in exponent form. The base is $1$ and the exponent is $7.$ \n\nThis means that $1$ is taken as a factor $7$ times. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{1}^{7}={{1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1}_{⏟}}_{7\\text{ times}}=1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
